        {
          "id": 2731157089,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Also, the variables in question are `unsigned int` not `int`; as per C18, \"A computation involving unsigned operands can never overflow, because a result that cannot be represented by the resulting unsigned integer type is reduced modulo the number that is one greater than the largest value that can be represented by the resulting type.\", and I think the Usual ~~Suspects~~Arithmetic Conversions turn `3` into `3U`.",
