        {
          "id": 2731379095,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The C23 description of the checked arithmetic macros says:\n\n> If these macros return false, the value assigned to *result correctly represents the mathematical result of the operation. Otherwise, these macros return true. In this case, the value assigned to *result is the mathematical result of the operation wrapped around to the width of *result.\n\nSince the unsigned integer operation is, as above, \"performed as if both operands were represented in a signed integer type with infinite range, and the result was then converted from this integer type to type1,\" the wrapped value does not \"correctly represent the mathematical result of the operation\" (in the sense of \"if performed in a signed integer type with infinite range\" - it's the correct mathematical result in the sense of after one has changed the semiring of unsigned integers into a ring modulo 2^N (ℤ/2^Nℤ for appropriate choice of N.)\n\nThe original proposal's Statement of the Problem makes it clear that unsigned integers wrapping around is something that it wanted to detect: https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg14/www/docs/n2466.pdf\n\nthough its use of \"overflow\" which, as you note, does not technically occur in the sense of how the C standard defines it results in attempts at clarifying the original proposal like https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg14/www/docs/n2837.pdf\n\nCommentary such as https://gustedt.wordpress.com/2022/12/18/checked-integer-arithmetic-in-the-prospect-of-c23/ and others seem to assume the practice. It would not make a lot of sense for the functions to always indicate success for unsigned integer types simply because wraparound is well-defined.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
