        {
          "id": 2731904296,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I'll look at filing a Clarification Report on that, to clarify that checked arithmetic macros on unsigned data types return `true` on wraparound.\n\nDoes <jtckdint.h> perform checked arithmetic with all the compilers we are likely to see (GNU Compiler Collection, LLVM family, Visual Studio, Oracle Studio, icc)? If not, we can't use it instead of doing the checks ourselves.\n\n> Should #20144 be backported to the actively maintained branches? Seems safe and sound.\n\nBackporting <jtckdint.h>, by itself, to the 4.4.x and 4.2.x branches, would have no effect whatsoever - it would add a header file that nobody includes - so it seems OK to do as a preparation for switching this fix to use C23 checked arithmetic. Backporting all of !19716 includes changes to 1) ftypes and 2) safe-math.h, which would be riskier.\n\nWith include/jtckdint.h backported, backporting a checked-arithmetic version of this change would change code that misbehaves on AIX-pcap files with FDDI packets to code that we hope would behave correctly on those files and behave the same for other files, so I think it's far more likely to introduce a fix than to introduce a bug.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-09-05T08:27:18.717Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-09-11T06:33:33.708Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 412622047,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "AndersBroman",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/132fb48f26018ea9516aea909144af3c3a94eaf2ba477efaa9a232abe80d322c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/AndersBroman"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2025-09-11T06:33:33.708Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 21202,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2732406513,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> Does <jtckdint.h> perform checked arithmetic with all the compilers we are likely to see (GNU Compiler Collection, LLVM family, Visual Studio, Oracle Studio, icc)?\n\nYes, it falls back to pure C11/C++11 implementations if necessary (it will use the C23 header if available, GCC built-ins if available), so it should work on any compiler as we require C11 and C++11. (It will emit a warning and the checks become no-ops if the compiler is compiling in C++ mode without C+11 or in C without C11.) I had to introduce a fix for Visual Studio to explicitly case to avoid some shortening warnings, which was accepted upstream as well.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-09-05T11:08:04.484Z",
