        {
          "id": 2732488574,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> (It will emit a warning and the checks become no-ops if the compiler is compiling in C++ mode without C+11 or in C without C11.)\n\nShould it just *fail* there?  If the checks are no-ops, that would mean that the integer wraparound wouldn't be detected and the excessively-large memory allocation would occur.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-09-05T11:40:54.122Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-09-11T06:33:33.708Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 412622047,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
