        {
          "id": 2732519836,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Presumably\n\n```\n#ifdef __has_include\n#define __ckd_has_include(x) __has_include(x)\n#else\n#define __ckd_has_include(x) 0\n#endif\n\n#if __ckd_has_include(<stdckdint.h>) && !defined(__cplusplus)\n#include <stdckdint.h>\n```\n\nworks because C23 has `__has_include`.\n\nVisual Studio C/C++ doesn't appear to have any builtins of the GCC/LLVM type, so presumably it'll fall back on the pure C11/C++11 implementation.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
